      "hasMediaInOriginal": false,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "Headline: Trezor Hits Back at ZachXBT: “Hardware Wallets Remain Strongest Self-Custody Option”\n\n- In a direct response to on-chain investigator ZachXBT’s earlier claim that “all hardware wallets are garbage and not recommended,” a Trezor executive emphasized that hardware wallets remain the strongest self-custody option for regular users.\n\nKey points:\n- The dispute centers on whether ordinary users should rely on hardware wallets versus other custody approaches amid ongoing debates about device security and recovery best practices.\n- Trezor’s position highlights the importance of keeping private keys offline and using trusted devices for signing transactions.\n- The exchange underscores broader industry tensions between hardcore security advocates and mainstream adoption narratives.\n\nWhat this means:\n- For most people, simplicity and reliability matter—hardware wallets aim to deliver both without requiring deep technical expertise.\n- Ongoing scrutiny will likely push manufacturers to improve documentation, recovery workflows, and transparency around firmware updates.\n\nBottom line: While no solution is perfect, the debate reinforces the need for clear guidance on self-custody for everyday crypto users.",
